The input you provided is already in the structured JSON format. However, if you want to convert it into the desired output format, you can use a programming language like Python. Here's an example:

```python
import json

input_str = "{"output_list": [
            {
                "function_name": "<function_name>",
                "vulnerability": "<vulnerability_type>",
                "reason": "<vulnerability_description>"
            }
        ]}"

# Remove unnecessary whitespace and newlines
input_str = input_str.replace(" ", "").replace("
", "")

# Convert the string to a dictionary
input_dict = json.loads(input_str)

# Convert the dictionary to the desired output format
output_dict = {
    "output_list": [
        {
            "function_name": "<function_name_1>",
            "vulnerability": "<short_vulnera_desc_1>",
            "reason": "<reason_1>"
        },
        {
            "function_name": "<function_name_2>",
            "vulnerability": "<short_vulnera_desc_2>",
            "reason": "<reason_2>"
        }
    ]
}

# Convert the dictionary to a JSON string
output_str = json.dumps(output_dict, indent=4)

print(output_str)
```

This code will output the desired JSON string:

```json
{
    "output_list": [
        {
            "function_name": "<function_name_1>",
            "vulnerability": "<short_vulnera_desc_1>",
            "reason": "<reason_1>"
        },
        {
            "function_name": "<function_name_2>",
            "vulnerability": "<short_vulnera_desc_2>",
            "reason": "<reason_2>"
        }
    ]
}
```

Note that you need to replace `<function_name_1>`, `<short_vulnera_desc_1>`, and `<reason_1>`, `<function_name_2>`, `<short_vulnera_desc_2>`, and `<reason_2>` with actual values.